{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"docs.branch.test serves the supplied documentation tree on node1 TCP port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Apache is active and listening on 8080. Requests using the docs host returned HTTP 200 for both index.html and handbook.txt, with response hashes matching the staged files before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cf6ef760868749e0","cmd-b14ee124dcd3427c","cmd-e82a79c8b7824383","cmd-2e153930ea2e4503"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"orders.branch.test serves the supplied purchasing tree on the same TCP port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The same name-based listener serves the orders host. Its index.html and catalog.csv returned HTTP 200 and hashes matching the staged files, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cf6ef760868749e0","cmd-b14ee124dcd3427c","cmd-e82a79c8b7824383","cmd-2e153930ea2e4503"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"An unknown Host header receives an error rather than either tenant's content.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An unknown Host header returned HTTP 403 before and after restart. Cross-tenant file requests also returned HTTP 404, supporting correct tenant isolation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f1868e9e39f34c92","cmd-e82a79c8b7824383","cmd-2e153930ea2e4503"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the approved content staged under /srv/legacy2/name-based-web-tenants.","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"All four files in the served docs and orders trees retained their baseline SHA-256 hashes through configuration and restart. However, the separately staged handover.txt file was not included in the final checksum observation, so preservation of the complete staged directory is not directly established.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-f61f847f4e554e7b","cmd-f1868e9e39f34c92","cmd-2e153930ea2e4503"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained RHEL 9.8 on kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8. Apache 2.4.62 and its dependencies were installed from configured RHEL 9 repositories, and the same OS and kernel were observed after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fef316870e134753","cmd-cceb520631e54bb7","cmd-2e153930ea2e4503","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.94,"summary":"Implementation mutations were causally related to installing and configuring the requested service, SELinux access, firewall access, and boot persistence. Package health remained good and no failed services were present. The only unwanted executor residue was a set of retained HTTP probe outputs: /tmp/unknown-host.out, /tmp/pre-docs, /tmp/pre-orders, /tmp/post-docs, /tmp/post-handbook, /tmp/post-orders, and /tmp/post-catalog. These bounded, low-risk evidence artifacts remained after completion rather than being cleaned up. The interrupted post-reboot probes were read-only and are not hygiene faults.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f1868e9e39f34c92","cmd-e82a79c8b7824383","cmd-2e153930ea2e4503","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The two name-based websites function correctly on their shared port, reject unknown hosts, and recovered cleanly after a verified node restart. The mandatory restart protocol is complete and coherent: healthy pre-restart service and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, connection loss was observed, a different boot ID was independently confirmed, and service, content, firewall, and rejection behavior recovered. The only task-evidence gap is that final preservation checks omitted handover.txt.","limitations":["No post-executor checksum or equivalent direct observation was captured for /srv/legacy2/name-based-web-tenants/handover.txt.","Lifecycle snapshots provide bounded platform, socket, package-health, failed-service, and temporary-file observations; they do not independently inventory all Apache, firewall, or SELinux configuration files."]}
